

⭐ CMB META‑EQUATION VISUALIZATION (Final Form)

The meta‑equation governs Ξ, the regime field.Visualization = showing how Ξ behaves, where it changes, and why it changes.

The viewer renders Ξ using three layers:

Regime Map

Regime Boundaries

Regime Events

Everything else is optional.

⭐ 1. Regime Map (Ξ Field → Color Regions)

This is the primary visualization of the meta‑equation.

Each Ξ regime gets a solid color:

CLASSICAL     → blue
RELATIVISTIC  → red
WARP          → purple
FROZEN        → cyan
SHEAR         → orange

Rendering rule:

Ξ(x,y) → color(x,y)

That’s it.

No gradients.No blending.Just pure regime identity.

This gives you the macro‑structure of the time fabric.

⭐ 2. Regime Boundaries (Ξ Changes → Contours)

Where Ξ changes from one regime to another, draw a boundary line.

Rendering rule:

if Ξ(x,y) != Ξ(x+1,y) or Ξ(x,y) != Ξ(x,y+1):
    draw boundary

Boundary style:

thin white line

slight glow

optional pulsing if unstable

This shows:

warp bubble edges

frozen pocket walls

classical → warp transitions

meta‑equation discontinuities

This is the skeleton of the meta‑equation.

⭐ 3. Regime Events (Ξ(t) → Timeline Markers)

Events are moments where the meta‑equation fires.

Examples:

regime switch

instability

collapse

ignition

freeze

shear onset

Rendering rule:

events[n] → timeline markers + viewport pulses

Viewer shows:

a vertical bar on the playback timeline

a brief pulse in the viewport

a highlight in the blueprint panel

This ties time, space, and blueprint logic together.

⭐ 4. Stability Visualization (Optional)

Ξ has "stability":

stable
metastable
unstable

Rendering:

stable → solid color

metastable → subtle noise texture

unstable → flicker or jitter

This makes the meta‑equation feel alive.

⭐ 5. Transition Visualization (Optional)

If "transition": true in the data:

Render a transition glow:

soft radial pulse

color = target regime

duration = 0.25–0.5s

This shows where and when the meta‑equation is switching.

⭐ 6. HUD Readout (Ξ at Cursor)

When the user hovers or probes:

Ξ: WARP
stability: metastable
transition: false

This is the meta‑equation inspector.

⭐ 7. Rendering Pipeline (Final Form)

draw regime map
draw regime boundaries
draw regime events
draw stability effects
draw transition pulses

Simple.Predictable.Fast.GPU‑friendly.



